From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wenziwanka <tech@wenziwanka.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 12:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tty-sdio: do not register the Bluetooth rfkill soft-blocked

rfkill_bluetooth_init() registers its switch with
rfkill_init_sw_state(true), i.e. soft-blocked, and nothing in the driver
ever unblocks it. On a board where the tty owner powers the WCN Bluetooth
subsystem when it opens /dev/ttyBT0, that block is stale from the start:
the hci device inherits it, bluetoothd sees a blocked adapter and refuses
to power it, and `btmgmt power on` fails. The same change has been
carried by the uwe5631 BT driver port for this reason.

Register the switch unblocked; userspace can still block it.

Signed-off-by: wenziwanka <tech@wenziwanka.com>
---

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/tty-sdio/rfkill.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/tty-sdio/rfkill.c
@@ -62,7 +62,12 @@
 		goto err_rfkill_alloc;
 	}
 	/* userspace cannot take exclusive control */
-	rfkill_init_sw_state(bt_rfk, true);
+	/*
+	 * The tty owner (btattach) powers the WCN Bluetooth subsystem when it
+	 * opens the port. Starting soft-blocked only leaves BlueZ looking at a
+	 * stale block and refusing to power the adapter; nothing ever clears it.
+	 */
+	rfkill_init_sw_state(bt_rfk, false);
 	rc = rfkill_register(bt_rfk);
 	if (rc)
 		goto err_rfkill_reg;
